  "notes": [
   "Page 1 shows steps 1-7 (chassis and cab). Wheels/tyres/axles are not yet shown.",
   "Black parts are hard to read in the illustration; the step 1 piece is taken as the black 2x6 plate with a yellow 1x2 plate at its end, and step 2 as the black 2x4 brick on it.",
   "Step 4 shows two yellow 1x2 plates falling onto the cab recess; interpreted as stacked (b8 on b7 on b4). Step 5 top plate is taken as one 2x4 plate (b9) resting on b6 and b8.",
   "Step 6: the ladder plate b10 is attached to the front of b5; the two yellow 1x3 bricks with clear round plates are assumed to sit on b5. The identity of these parts is a best guess from the parts list.",
   "Step 7 wedge plate b15 is assumed to rest on b9 and b6.",
   "The piece-to-piece 'rests_on' relationships are recorded as joined edges with no port detail.",
   "Step 8 flips the model upside down; the two wheel-holder plates (b16, b17) clutch the underside of the black 2x6 plate b1 (they are joined to b1 only).",
   "Step 9: the two 1x4 bricks (b18, b19) are taken as sitting on the yellow sloped brick b4, and the 1x4 plate b20 on the front wedge b15. The exact supports are a best guess from the leftover parts list.",
   "Step 10: the trans-clear 1x2 plate b21 goes on b20 and the yellow 1x2 plate b22 on top of it, as the inset shows.",
   "Step 11: the yellow 2x4 plate b23 (the dump bed top) is taken as resting on b18 and b19. It carries two trans-red round plates (b24, b25).",
   "Step 12: four wheels with tyres go onto the holder plates, two per plate (axle-hole.1 and axle-hole.2). Which wheel goes on which side is not distinguished.",
   "Steps 8 and 12 show no other building steps. The final photo adds nothing."
  ]
 },
